# 🟡 Level 2 – How It Works

## What Happens When You Visit a Website?

Suppose you type:

```text
www.google.com
```

The sequence is:

```text
Browser
   ↓
DNS Lookup
   ↓
IP Address Returned
   ↓
Router
   ↓
Internet
   ↓
Google Server
   ↓
HTTPS Response
   ↓
Webpage Loads
```

---

# DHCP (Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol)

Imagine a college hostel.

Every student needs a room.

Instead of choosing rooms randomly, the warden assigns one.

DHCP works the same way—it automatically assigns:

* IP Address
* Subnet Mask
* Default Gateway
* DNS Server

Without DHCP, you'd have to configure every device manually.

---

# DNS (Domain Name System)

Humans remember names.

Computers use numbers.

DNS translates:

```text
google.com
```

into

```text
142.250.xx.xx
```

### Without DNS

You would have to remember the IP address of every website!

---

# Subnet Mask

A subnet mask tells your computer:

* Which part of the IP identifies the **network**
* Which part identifies the **host (device)**

Example:

```text
IP Address:
192.168.1.25

Subnet Mask:
255.255.255.0
```

This means:

* Network: 192.168.1
* Host: 25

We'll study subnetting in greater depth later because it's a common interview topic.

